[Music]  in this video we will learn how to  deploy google's external https load  balancer with terraform  first let's have a quick overview of  https load balancers  google cloud offers global and regional  https load balancing with internal and  external ip addresses  these load balancers scale as the users  and traffic grow thus providing seamless  auto scaling  they can balance http and https traffic  across multiple backend instances across  multiple regions  now let's understand what terraform is  terraform is an infrastructure as a code  tool that automates the provisioning and  management of infrastructure  it allows users to define infrastructure  in human readable configuration files  that can be easily versioned reused and  shared  terraform is a platform agnostic tool  that is it can be used across any  supported provider  it accomplishes this by interacting with  the apis of cloud providers  now we will look at the benefits of  terraform  terraform can manage infrastructure on  multiple cloud platforms such as google  cloud platform or gcp azure and aws just  to name a few  the human readable configuration  language helps you write infrastructure  code quickly  it allows you to track infrastructure  changes through version control  in today's demo we will focus on how to  deploy an external https load balancer  that forwards traffic to two google  compute engine virtual machines  created as part of instance group 1  and instance group 2 in u.s best 1 and  u.s east 1 regions with terraform  before we deploy the load balancer with  terraform ensure that the terraform  service account used for deploying the  resources has the relevant iem  permissions  here are the required rules  compute load balancer admin role  compute network admin role  compute security admin role  and compute instance admin role  now it's time for the demo  open cloud shell and set the project  using gcloud config where you want to  deploy the resources  note  terraform is integrated with cloud shell  and cloud shell automatically  authenticates terraform letting you get  started with less setup  navigate to the directory where the  terraform script is located  in our example the terraform script is  located under directory home test cloud  shell underscore open  terraform hyphen google hyphen lb hyphen  http  next step is to initialize the working  directory with terraform init command  it initializes the working directory  containing terraform configuration files  it also performs several different  initialization steps to prepare a  working directory for use  now let's look at the terraform script  main.tf  in this script we have defined the  resources we want to deploy global  forwarding rule  multiple manage instance groups and url  map  finally  run terraform apply to execute the  script and deploy the resources  let's now validate if all the resources  are created successfully and we are able  to access the load balancer ip  in the google cloud console go to the  load balancing page and validate that  the load balancer resource is created  in our example you can see the load  balancer multi hyphen make hyphen lb  hyphen http hyphen url hyphen map is  created  click on load balancer and verify that  the back-ends are healthy  great we can see all the back-ends are  healthy  click on back-ends to verify that there  are two instance groups one each in the  u.s east one and u.s west 1 region  access load balancer ip by navigating to  http  34.111.126.202 from your browser and  validate that you are able to access the  backends  congratulations  we have successfully created an external  https load balancer with terraform and  verified that all the resources are  created and the load balancer is  accessible  check out this documentation for sample  terraform scripts that can be used to  deploy external https load balancers for  your preferred backend type  [Music]  you

